AVLO: wasm-gc trampoline — test the 2-arg shape first (2, 3, 1, 0).

METH_VARARGS, METH_O, METH_NOARGS and getset getters all cross the
trampoline as 2-arg calls; 3-arg is only METH_VARARGS|METH_KEYWORDS.
Upstream tests 3-arg first, so the majority of calls pay one wasted
ref.test. The compiled module hex regenerates from this source during
the cpython build (emscripten_trampoline_inner.wasm ->
emscripten_trampoline_wasm.c), so no other file changes.

Applied by cpython/Makefile's .patched rule (cat patches/*.patch |
patch -p1) after upstream 0001-0009; staged there by build.sh's
patches/cpython/ lane, which nukes the build tree on any lane change.

--- a/Python/emscripten_trampoline_inner.c
+++ b/Python/emscripten_trampoline_inner.c
@@ -30,9 +30,12 @@
 {
   *success = 1;
-  TRY_RETURN_CALL(three_arg, self, args, kw);
-  TRY_RETURN_CALL(two_arg, self, args);
+  // AVLO: 2-arg first — METH_VARARGS / METH_O / METH_NOARGS and getset
+  // getters all cross as 2-arg; 3-arg is only METH_VARARGS|METH_KEYWORDS.
+  // Testing the common shape first saves one ref.test on the hottest calls.
+  TRY_RETURN_CALL(two_arg, self, args);
+  TRY_RETURN_CALL(three_arg, self, args, kw);
   TRY_RETURN_CALL(one_arg, self);
   TRY_RETURN_CALL(zero_arg);
   *success = 0;
   return 0;
 }
